rian, he made famous contributions to logic, mathematics, physics, and metaphysics, yet viewed his own aspirations as ultimately ethical and theological, and married these theoretical concerns with politics, diplomacy, and an equally broad range of practical reforms: juridical, economic, administrative, technological, medical, and ecclesiastical. Maria Rosa Antognazza's pioneering biography not only surveys the full breadth and depth of these theoretical interests and practical activities, it also weaves them together for the first time into a unified portrait of this unique thinker and the world from which he came.","thumbnailUrl":"/book-covers/book-leibniz-an-intellectual-biography-maria-rosa-antognazza.jpg","displaySummary":"Of all the thinkers of the century of genius that inaugurated modern philosophy, none lived an intellectual life more rich and varied than Gottfried Wilhelm Leibniz (1646-1716). Trained as a jurist and employed as a counsellor, librarian, and historian, he made famous contributions to logic, mathematics, physics, and metaphysics, yet viewed his own aspirations as ultimately ethical and theological, and married these theoretical concerns with politics, diplomacy, and an equally broad range of practical reforms: juridical, economic, administrative, technological, medical, and ecclesiastical. Maria Rosa Antognazza's pioneering biography not only surveys the full breadth and depth of these theoretical interests and practical activities, it also weaves them together for the first time into a unified portrait of this unique thinker and the world from which he came.","primarySubject":"Science","primaryTopic":"Business, Capitalism & Corporations","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"Science","confidence":"low","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"Science","score":6,"evidenceCount":3},{"subject":"Business & Economics","score":5,"evidenceCount":3},{"subject":"History","score":4,"evidenceCount":4},{"subject":"Medicine & Public Health","sc